<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gododdin</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 638 CE (approx.) · capital Din Eidyn (Edinburgh)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British kingdom of Lothian centred on Edinburgh, celebrated in the early Welsh poem Y Gododdin, which fell to Northumbria in the 7th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gododdin was the post-Roman kingdom of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/votadini">Votadini</a>, whose name became Guotodin and then Gododdin in Welsh. Its centre was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/din-eidyn">Din Eidyn</a>, the rock of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, and it stretched across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothian">Lothian</a> and the eastern Borders. Welsh tradition also linked the district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manaw-gododdin">Manaw Gododdin</a>, around the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firth-of-forth">Forth</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunedda">Cunedda</a>, legendary founder of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom is best known from Y Gododdin, attributed to the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aneirin">Aneirin</a>, which mourns a war band feasted for a year by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mynyddog-mwynfawr">Mynyddog Mwynfawr</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/din-eidyn">Din Eidyn</a> and then slaughtered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-catraeth">Catraeth</a>, usually identified as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catterick">Catterick</a>, around 600. The poem portrays an aristocratic warrior society bound by loyalty, mead and gifts. Hillforts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/traprain-law">Traprain Law</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castle-rock-edinburgh">Edinburgh Castle Rock</a> were key centres.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Anglian kingdom of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bernicia">Bernicia</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Northumbria</a>, expanded northward in the 7th century. Irish annals record the siege of Etin in 638, generally taken as the Northumbrian capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothian">Lothian</a> remained English until it passed to the Scottish kings in the 10th and 11th centuries.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 450 CE – 638 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.66%;width:3.74%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 638 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Din Eidyn (Edinburgh)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mynyddog Mwynfawr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic, Cumbric</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gododdin, Guotodin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=544&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gododdin" aria-label="Kingdom of Gododdin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4623 286 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gododdin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4942 527h0M4945 553h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4943 542h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d=